[{"id":"VRCE-4-26-1","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":26,"verse":1,"english":"On Sugrīva being installed and the monkeys entering the cave, Rāma, along with his younger brother, got at the Prasravana hill, resounded with the noise of tigers and deer, filled with terrible lions, covered with diverse trees, creepers and bowers, inhabited by bears, monkeys, Gopucyas and cats, resembling a collection of clouds and always auspicious.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-27-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4026001","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c553f8b4a7eda93d9d54f4c60498469d86039c30d24f8dae58693e412c8de239","compact":"1a1862bee26115b2ba8ed2e5835bfb6726d6460f7921f6fd172350169040bd6c","nasal":"1a1862bee26115b2ba8ed2e5835bfb6726d6460f7921f6fd172350169040bd6c"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-26-2","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":26,"verse":2,"english":"On Sugrīva being installed and the monkeys entering the cave, Rāma, along with his younger brother, got at the Prasravana hill, resounded with the noise of tigers and deer, filled with terrible lions, covered with diverse trees, creepers and bowers, inhabited by bears, monkeys, Gopucyas and cats, resembling a collection of clouds and always auspicious.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.77,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-27-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4026002","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"07e23833a7d0535479fd17cf1fcea1a5b75f5bc9f7b9b1dec697478e7ae30d78","compact":"7abb43c8798fc1df8ceda65544a3144ec9f42d2cd2fb23e20442c643bc1492fb","nasal":"7abb43c8798fc1df8ceda65544a3144ec9f42d2cd2fb23e20442c643bc1492fb"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-26-3","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":26,"verse":3,"english":"On Sugrīva being installed and the monkeys entering the cave, Rāma, along with his younger brother, got at the Prasravana hill, resounded with the noise of tigers and deer, filled with terrible lions, covered with diverse trees, creepers and bowers, inhabited by bears, monkeys, Gopucyas and cats, resembling a collection of clouds and always auspicious.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.662,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-27-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4026003","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"adcfc0a46df7587853057da159e73d884984e79a6f2be7353e2abd8d8e80222a","compact":"4f590382313a867cda46b1b3b0de97869e1913a97de097c0a5c18972b8aac2bb","nasal":"2e25e7fb10b1e9335241533810c5043d0c883c70e1abc5c0da5c044e9d3e4848"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-26-4","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":26,"verse":4,"english":"Rāma, along with Saumitri, selected for his habitation, a spacious cave, situated on the summit of that hill.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.85,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-27-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4026004","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d595669ec977669ab76bec24abd35db4cb337ea01981e01ef9da0a1394b4f986","compact":"70db21e7dbac7551d3c1347b730e1030a268ed3e795fb94f6baac9f72f593ba5","nasal":"a511f2fc0723b4b4a29615e9856fde05263ade44e6b0ee01df35dd46e806fe83"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-26-5","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":26,"verse":5,"english":"Having said this, Rāghava, along with Laks maņa, dwelt in that Prasravana hill abounding in caves and bowers.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.571,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-27-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4026005","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f260c46cdfde7b14310fba9f81bfd9325c8c7239c9f69823e7211faf1fa327a2","compact":"9857cee4a592034daf6f0f5dbb69cd11ffa557d37dbcef9baf6f5ff66b772e76","nasal":"a4f5c8e150f971c9ee2caa6d9ea49b98f5c8de51afe85573f03790493c2fa7e4"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-26-6","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":26,"verse":6,"english":"He did not attain to a best felicity although he lived in that pleasant hill filled with many things.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.929,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-27-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4026006","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4ea63c200e88bf949397e2d29cb01d90f6d13e7a6140b5b8392d56aea3ad3fc4","compact":"54d561b959c7860d33d123bc7536af4efbb6a4d996168b097b6fc8da2a318f58","nasal":"54d561b959c7860d33d123bc7536af4efbb6a4d996168b097b6fc8da2a318f58"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-26-7","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":26,"verse":7,"english":"Pondering over the ravishment of his spouse, dearer than his life, beholding the setting of the Sun in particular, he did not go to sleep, although he laid himself on the bed in the night.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-27-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4026007","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f04940789fbe0b11a69a3a34da11e5b1885162f5f49520e5ca1d40207cff9530","compact":"60ffca7f6c84ff5ca1ec9e057b4a372f20480168ecc92b897450fbbc1d2d888c","nasal":"a00a8246650e34038fe896d8c3f37d22443d2df75b5fc03524a8a12f2f273757"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-26-8","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":26,"verse":8,"english":"His younger brother Laksmana, equally aggrieved, spoke to Kākutstha, thus bewailing being exercised with grief and almost beside himself with sorrow, consequent upon Sita's bereavement, saying.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.776,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-27-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4026008","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e816d1139eca8ae196f96f7671c63f2b30893cf1d6a7ab1712627e70d47daf8a","compact":"5448df142fad47b143e38ab25deeb67635ce3c6368534996afd57f3b1660c4f6","nasal":"5448df142fad47b143e38ab25deeb67635ce3c6368534996afd57f3b1660c4f6"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-26-9","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":26,"verse":9,"english":"It does not behove you to lament thus, being exercised with grief—it is not unknown to you that people, thus bewailing do exhaust themselves by and by.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.871,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-27-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4026009","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0a54a55cae4f71b377f72626f7b84e2a89b5fad119ffc468797445323e1addc0","compact":"ffa2643ed2d45577a05a7a563ff0ae079b87ccfb06975483c2902f370635c095","nasal":"398a1244e113ac84fd89d6231e30fdbb7e9ab8e5862fb1780fbbca3c2d4d2d97"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-26-10","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":26,"verse":10,"english":"O Rāghava, you are devoted to pious actions and the services of the Deity in this world-and pious, energetic and did believe in the existence of God.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-27-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4026010","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1cb7c21c330239a28a438eecaabb2deba4b3aa33a0a41e339f8c731c676e1e26","compact":"b099294ebeb3a7948dbbc2609a084b6d905351002ff0fddd23791ead491ff7f5","nasal":"b791c0fda963121496dc67b9138d3b00c7bd057c2c68d398d5cedc498bb6975e"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-26-11","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":26,"verse":11,"english":"Without being persevering you shall not be able to destroy in conflict your enemy—that terrible, wily Rākşasa.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.735,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-27-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4026011","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"39f70caeed4c632f8c95b741ea2111a0accec7c7d2dbba2753db0d750510b686","compact":"d76cf37c779654c9343a6a5381d5ed0ede9a3ba3e3198cfd86b7d0d7360ba2c7","nasal":"b98ecf7177e80f7a9613584a64b788ec611e13e0c6e8740bdf3be32d9187d159"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-26-12","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":26,"verse":12,"english":"Do you renounce your grief and take recourse to energy and you shall be able to slay that Rākş asa with all his family.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.55,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-27-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4026012","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cc30c078da55a0a2499ee1d0055cb8353b8e66b69114fe12e8a3cc6782dad39f","compact":"4c93638ebf4cba76b347403f3d2b641563431d1bc1213c520ee15022da6988e3","nasal":"4c93638ebf4cba76b347403f3d2b641563431d1bc1213c520ee15022da6988e3"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-26-13","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":26,"verse":13,"english":"What of the destruction of Rāvana, you are O Kākutstha. capable of uprooting the earth with oceans, forest and hills.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.768,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-27-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4026013","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b940a86c46c59086fa747db2d7f33410897a05839edcae0a3efe588716198b1d","compact":"6b1229bbe2bc95060a21456e3ee9a3fa1138705ff160533bd15d80b2883523c5","nasal":"2c6c37b3318c91f496d429ebe60011e595579fa9f9b278e445d08e82d5d254a8"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-26-14","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":26,"verse":14,"english":"I, too, am exciting your latent energy like to fire hidden in ashes with oblations.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-27-30"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4026014","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"65f20766ed28709a66f46669da87a006ebdd9f73618c74aac6b3fd4056965ac9","compact":"27da03798f40a24729f681168ab7dfce9b23b489c6442da3ffdc0e31cff32f12","nasal":"0c1781bba6b784e16eb2f2b555c16b2a4fcd26e42410a0532a219305898d203a"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-26-15","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":26,"verse":15,"english":"Welcoming the auspicious and well-meaning accents of Lakşmaņa, Raghava again spoke to him the following affectionate words. when you","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.864,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-27-31"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4026015","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bd61b39ae941163f82d9d07e9664c1013a2debd8609bdd3e54b9b05765e9d759","compact":"727d817cdb70a60663e9924693535b10e5f12453a4a6d66194b5cb3a823a4978","nasal":"727d817cdb70a60663e9924693535b10e5f12453a4a6d66194b5cb3a823a4978"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-26-16","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":26,"verse":16,"english":"O Lakşmaņa, truly do your words become you, affectionate, devoted, truthful and intent in my welfare as you are.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-27-32"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4026016","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2eff7b567bc33f5ebc240d5b910f1fcfc88dec33a0c04185d5dc394cc41c9dee","compact":"683f3a88a2c7473d10447f247539f07c61e36e5e6a525d03b59e5b0ae967d6b7","nasal":"683f3a88a2c7473d10447f247539f07c61e36e5e6a525d03b59e5b0ae967d6b7"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-26-17","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":26,"verse":17,"english":"Renouncing this grief standing in the way of all business, I shail call forth, the more, this my energy on the occasion of displaying my prowess.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-27-33"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4026017","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2f91837f71ea3947eebde0dc6b0b5511dc944646693a066194d32d717e1177c9","compact":"afda4c981cb4b3a3a62e30554cb9245c2738fc9432986ba90e304511b6afa908","nasal":"afda4c981cb4b3a3a62e30554cb9245c2738fc9432986ba90e304511b6afa908"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-26-18","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":26,"verse":18,"english":"Rains have set in and do you wait for the autumn shall encompass the destruction of Rāvana with his kingdom and kinsmen.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.197,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-27-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4026018","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4255b6c047df1265acad2d8701b4e35c593cb95f7f410d46a60b6c108a85f0f0","compact":"e83bb2a932dc07dd744cbd4e122b0aad311282e97c24cad9c69d0ffa8cf53a4a","nasal":"e83bb2a932dc07dd744cbd4e122b0aad311282e97c24cad9c69d0ffa8cf53a4a"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-26-19","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":26,"verse":19,"english":"Hearing these words of Hanumān, said on a very proper occasion, the intelligent Sugrīva, made up his mind for a worthy end.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.164,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-29-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4026019","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bc756732c9b1f861b6654e0089e5ccb3681b97d929397fc5e190f5569ffda8d1","compact":"31a02c33bf08ea05d3457e5cd54ea738041044a2ab666598da3943f62395a0cf","nasal":"9ca30